WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.156 --> 00:00:01.257
(crowd applauds)

00:00:01.257 --> 00:00:02.278
- Thank you.

00:00:02.278 --> 00:00:04.863
Oh, those are bright lights.

00:00:04.863 --> 00:00:05.696
- Uh.

00:00:06.948 --> 00:00:07.781
- Um.

00:00:07.781 --> 00:00:08.741
(whooshing)

00:00:08.741 --> 00:00:09.840
(squeaking)

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:12.491
(expectant music)

00:00:12.491 --> 00:00:14.899
- My name is Jared, this
is my daughter Flynn.

00:00:14.899 --> 00:00:17.272
I guess I'm gonna be tryin'
some stand-up this week.

00:00:17.272 --> 00:00:18.105
Ah, ah.

00:00:19.866 --> 00:00:21.189
Mmm, thank you.

00:00:21.189 --> 00:00:22.932
- Hi, I'm Auri and this is my dad.

00:00:22.932 --> 00:00:23.976
- Hi, I'm Cedric.

00:00:23.976 --> 00:00:25.581
- He does do a lot of dad jokes

00:00:25.581 --> 00:00:27.747
that we started calling groaners,

00:00:27.747 --> 00:00:29.698
because they're so bad
they make you groan.

00:00:29.698 --> 00:00:31.063
- No, I have not done comedy.

00:00:31.063 --> 00:00:32.143
I've seen a lot of comedy.

00:00:32.143 --> 00:00:34.577
Entertained the notion
once, I wrote a page down

00:00:34.577 --> 00:00:36.301
and I threw it out 'cause it was terrible.

00:00:36.301 --> 00:00:37.134
- Do I think I'm funny?

00:00:37.134 --> 00:00:39.361
Even a broken clock is right twice a day,

00:00:39.361 --> 00:00:41.619
so I guess, yeah, I guess I
hit it every once in awhile.

00:00:41.619 --> 00:00:42.968
(bell chimes)

00:00:42.968 --> 00:00:43.908
- She likes that voice.

00:00:43.908 --> 00:00:44.811
Flynn,

00:00:44.811 --> 00:00:45.970
are you sure?

00:00:45.970 --> 00:00:47.303
(Flynn laughs)

00:00:47.303 --> 00:00:49.499
See, she thinks I'm funny.

00:00:49.499 --> 00:00:53.582
(exciting electric guitar music)

00:00:56.058 --> 00:00:57.871
- I thought I had a week,
how am I gonna do this?

00:00:57.871 --> 00:01:00.538
Both having a job and being a father?

00:01:00.538 --> 00:01:01.719
See how hard this is?

00:01:01.719 --> 00:01:02.950
- I'm pretty nervous about it actually.

00:01:02.950 --> 00:01:06.718
Might wanna have a medic
standing by, seriously.

00:01:06.718 --> 00:01:08.945
- I've got 72 hours to
write a five minute set.

00:01:08.945 --> 00:01:11.644
- Okay, and you need dad jokes?

00:01:11.644 --> 00:01:13.988
What do you say when you
meet a deer with no eyes?

00:01:13.988 --> 00:01:15.079
- What do you say?

00:01:15.079 --> 00:01:16.872
- I have no eye deer.

00:01:16.872 --> 00:01:18.228
- Your dad was proud of that one, too?

00:01:18.228 --> 00:01:20.664
- Yeah, he loved it, totally.
- That's good.

00:01:20.664 --> 00:01:21.802
- Mommy!

00:01:21.802 --> 00:01:23.283
- I just wrote all of
my material last night

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:25.082
and this is like, tomorrow night.

00:01:25.082 --> 00:01:27.379
I'll be amongst some seasoned comedians

00:01:27.379 --> 00:01:29.010
who probably are gonna kill it.

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:31.014
- So I'm gonna do my set for my family.

00:01:31.014 --> 00:01:33.205
My wife didn't know if she
was gonna be a good mother.

00:01:33.205 --> 00:01:34.347
How are you supposed to know

00:01:34.347 --> 00:01:35.524
if you're gonna be a good mom?
- Mommy!

00:01:35.524 --> 00:01:37.163
Oh, but as soon as the baby fell out,

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:40.184
and the did fall out, my
wife wanted the baby out,

00:01:40.184 --> 00:01:41.017
and the baby fell out-
- You're gonna share

00:01:41.017 --> 00:01:42.333
that information?
- Yes.

00:01:42.333 --> 00:01:44.639
- I did look up this article online,

00:01:44.639 --> 00:01:47.765
basically it says, six ways not to suck

00:01:47.765 --> 00:01:48.598
doing a stand-up routine.

00:01:48.598 --> 00:01:49.703
And I figured reading that, you know,

00:01:49.703 --> 00:01:53.225
I'm probably gonna do all of those.

00:01:53.225 --> 00:01:56.530
- We're still really nervous
but I walked around the block

00:01:56.530 --> 00:01:58.312
kind of rehearsing my set in my head

00:01:58.312 --> 00:02:00.381
and that made it a little easier.

00:02:00.381 --> 00:02:03.623
Right now, I am just kinda writing down

00:02:03.623 --> 00:02:06.497
key elements from my set, just so I can

00:02:06.497 --> 00:02:08.321
try to remember it better.

00:02:08.321 --> 00:02:09.548
I'll probably bring it on the stage

00:02:09.548 --> 00:02:10.969
just so I don't get lost.

00:02:10.969 --> 00:02:12.839
- You know, in life,
the rewards go to those

00:02:12.839 --> 00:02:14.568
that are in the arena fighting.

00:02:14.568 --> 00:02:18.086
So if I get up there, having
never done something like this,

00:02:18.086 --> 00:02:20.819
just the act of trying, I got
something to feel good about.

00:02:20.819 --> 00:02:22.613
(ominous music)

00:02:22.613 --> 00:02:24.332
- I am a little nervous about the show.

00:02:24.332 --> 00:02:25.515
There might be long pauses,

00:02:25.515 --> 00:02:27.308
and it's gonna be kinda awkward,

00:02:27.308 --> 00:02:28.666
but I've got a plan for that.

00:02:28.666 --> 00:02:31.218
- Lots could go wrong,
jokes might not land,

00:02:31.218 --> 00:02:33.796
I might just forget stuff.

00:02:33.796 --> 00:02:35.156
I am not ready.

00:02:35.156 --> 00:02:36.098
I made a mistake.

00:02:36.098 --> 00:02:38.205
I will regret everything.

00:02:38.205 --> 00:02:41.939
(audience cheering)

00:02:41.939 --> 00:02:42.939
- Thank you.

00:02:44.521 --> 00:02:45.786
Alright.

00:02:45.786 --> 00:02:48.119
Oh, those are bright lights.

00:02:49.061 --> 00:02:49.894
- Uh.

00:02:52.682 --> 00:02:53.821
- Um.

00:02:53.821 --> 00:02:55.354
Just a shout out to everyone out here,

00:02:55.354 --> 00:02:57.956
you're all a beautiful
crowd. (audience cheers)

00:02:57.956 --> 00:02:59.185
I just want you to know that.

00:02:59.185 --> 00:03:00.914
Yeah, something, you know, that this is

00:03:00.914 --> 00:03:02.274
a really an interesting experience.

00:03:02.274 --> 00:03:04.310
I'm getting a little lightheaded, um.

00:03:04.310 --> 00:03:07.206
(laughs) I guess that's part of

00:03:07.206 --> 00:03:09.010
the whole stand-up experience.

00:03:09.010 --> 00:03:12.971
Nominative determinism,
anyone ever heard of that one?

00:03:12.971 --> 00:03:14.528
I had no idea what it
was, I had to look it up.

00:03:14.528 --> 00:03:17.499
Anyway, really quick, it's the uh,

00:03:17.499 --> 00:03:19.999
hypothesis that your name, um,

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:23.509
influences your life choices.

00:03:23.509 --> 00:03:25.551
So, you know, like if your, you know,

00:03:25.551 --> 00:03:27.667
your name is Seymour Skinmore

00:03:27.667 --> 00:03:31.061
you'll probably end up
becoming a dermatologist.

00:03:31.061 --> 00:03:32.587
You know, like the anasthesiologist,

00:03:32.587 --> 00:03:35.170
Dr. Feelgood, obviously, right.

00:03:36.639 --> 00:03:39.165
Some low hanging fruit, there.

00:03:39.165 --> 00:03:41.652
The, uh, another one is, you know

00:03:41.652 --> 00:03:44.369
like Dr. Bonewell would
be a chiropractor, right,

00:03:44.369 --> 00:03:45.758
oh, oops. (audience laughs)

00:03:45.758 --> 00:03:48.250
That could also be
something else, couldn't it?

00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:49.083
Oh well.

00:03:49.083 --> 00:03:51.880
- You ever just look at
someone and you're pretty sure,

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:54.949
but you're not sure,
but you don't wanna ask

00:03:54.949 --> 00:03:58.003
'cause it might be racist,
like if they're a ninja?

00:03:58.003 --> 00:03:59.679
(audience laughs)

00:03:59.679 --> 00:04:01.625
Well, I found out a good way to figure out

00:04:01.625 --> 00:04:03.485
if someone's a ninja, you just like,

00:04:03.485 --> 00:04:05.483
throw a knife at their face.

00:04:05.483 --> 00:04:06.316
And if they catch it,

00:04:06.316 --> 00:04:07.445
oh shit, that dude's a ninja,

00:04:07.445 --> 00:04:09.605
if they don't, you just
stabbed someone in the face.

00:04:09.605 --> 00:04:11.207
But if you think someone's a ninja,

00:04:11.207 --> 00:04:13.236
they're probably a ninja,
you know what I mean?

00:04:13.236 --> 00:04:14.440
(audience laughs)

00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:15.273
Yeah.

00:04:16.370 --> 00:04:18.285
My wife didn't like that joke either.

00:04:18.285 --> 00:04:19.657
Uh.

00:04:19.657 --> 00:04:22.222
Yeah, she also didn't know whether or not

00:04:22.222 --> 00:04:23.501
she'd be a good mom,

00:04:23.501 --> 00:04:25.326
but when the baby fell out,

00:04:25.326 --> 00:04:26.811
(audience laughs)

00:04:26.811 --> 00:04:29.615
her maternal instincts
kicked in, she's a great mom.

00:04:29.615 --> 00:04:31.983
And I think my paternal
instincts kicked in, too.

00:04:31.983 --> 00:04:35.276
I became very protective
and I immediately regretted

00:04:35.276 --> 00:04:36.859
not knowing a martial art

00:04:36.859 --> 00:04:40.842
because there are all those
ninjas out there, you know?

00:04:40.842 --> 00:04:41.737
They're dangerous.

00:04:41.737 --> 00:04:44.746
Like even, not just the asian ones.

00:04:44.746 --> 00:04:47.919
Like, American ninjas
might be more dangerous

00:04:47.919 --> 00:04:50.059
'cause of white privilege.

00:04:50.059 --> 00:04:53.444
(exciting rock music)

00:04:53.444 --> 00:04:54.425
- You did great.

00:04:54.425 --> 00:04:55.333
You really did good.
- Thank you.

00:04:55.333 --> 00:04:56.511
Yeah, your timing was excellent.

00:04:56.511 --> 00:04:57.969
- I kinda blacked out.

00:04:57.969 --> 00:04:58.929
- I got a little lightheaded

00:04:58.929 --> 00:04:59.938
there for a moment.
- Yeah.

00:04:59.938 --> 00:05:02.423
I'd probably do this again, I was thinking

00:05:02.423 --> 00:05:06.418
about my performance in
relationship to the actual comedians

00:05:06.418 --> 00:05:09.340
who were very professional,
they were really, really good.

00:05:09.340 --> 00:05:10.844
So it made me realize
I had a long way to go,

00:05:10.844 --> 00:05:13.866
but it's kind of inspired
actually, you know,

00:05:13.866 --> 00:05:15.883
so who knows, maybe I would
do something like this again.

00:05:15.883 --> 00:05:17.503
- I'm not gonna do it again.

00:05:17.503 --> 00:05:18.568
I'm not gonna do stand-up.

00:05:18.568 --> 00:05:22.179
I'm not gonna do it again,
you don't have to worry.

00:05:22.179 --> 00:05:24.373
- So I just saw my dad perform

00:05:24.373 --> 00:05:27.256
and I think he did a really good job.

00:05:27.256 --> 00:05:29.231
I'm proud of you, you did a good job.

00:05:29.231 --> 00:05:30.148
I love you.

00:05:36.373 --> 00:05:37.456
(whooshing)

00:05:37.456 --> 00:05:38.613
(creaking)

